    <a href="nest.html">Nest</a>
    <a href="marks.html">Marks</a>
    <a href="kraehes_kalls.html">Krähe's Kalls</a>
    <a href="KriegForeKaster.html">ForeKaster</a>
    <a href="KriegForeKaster_compendium.html">Compendium</a>
    <a href="ohrwurm.html">Ohrwurm</a>
    <a class="cta" href="ledger.html">The Ledger</a>
  </div>
</div></nav>

<header class="hero-wrap"><div class="wrap"><div class="hero">
  <div class="rv in">
    <div class="kicker">The Prescient Desk™ · Instrument under public test</div>
    <h1>Retro-Prescient Audit<span class="tm">™</span></h1>
    <p class="dek">A method for telling foresight from arithmetic. Forecasts sealed before
    their outcomes, adjudicated blind, and scored on a record that keeps its own misses —
    permanently, in public.</p>
    <p class="motto">Calling our shots in the fog. Soaring through our misses.</p>
    <p style="font:500 .7rem var(--mono,monospace);letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--dim,#8b8b85);margin:.9rem 0 0">Retro-Prescient Audit™ — the method &nbsp;·&nbsp; The Prescient Desk™ — the instrument that runs it</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn primary" href="ledger.html">Read the Ledger</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="#method">The Method</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="leuchte" role="img" aria-label="The NebelKrähe sigil within sighting rings, a slow light sweeping the fog behind it">
    <div class="beam" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    
    <svg class="rings" viewBox="0 0 400 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="192"/>
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="158" class="mark"/>
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="122"/>
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="88" class="mark"/>
      <text x="200" y="16" text-anchor="middle">SEALED · ADJUDICATED · SCORED</text>
      <text x="200" y="386" text-anchor="middle">DIE KRÄHE SIEHT DURCH DEN NEBEL</text>
    <g id="contacts"></g><text id="scope-ticker" class="ticker" x="200" y="264" text-anchor="middle" style="opacity:0" aria-hidden="true"></text></svg>
    <div class="crow-orbit" aria-hidden="true"><img class="crow-mark" src="crow_mark_small.svg" alt=""></div>
    <div class="hub" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</div></div></header>

<div class="band" aria-label="Live record"><div class="band-in" id="band">
  <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">Issued</span><span class="val" id="b-issued">—</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">Open</span><span class="val" id="b-open">—</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">Hits / Misses</span><span class="val" id="b-hm">—</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">Brier</span><span class="val brass" id="b-brier">—</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">Voided</span><span class="val" id="b-void">—</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><span class="lbl">War Desk A/B</span><span class="val" id="b-wd">—</span></div><div class="stat"><span class="lbl">War Desk pull</span><span class="val" id="wardesk-asof">—</span></div>
  <span class="asof" id="b-asof">Live from the ledger</span>
  <a class="go" href="ledger.html">Full record →</a>
</div></div>

<div class="siegel" aria-label="Live commitment seal">
  <div class="siegel-track" id="siegel-track">
    <span class="siegel-run" id="siegel-run">COMMITMENT SEAL · SHA-256(ledger.json) · computing…</span>
  </div>
</div>

<main class="wrap">

<section id="method">
  <div class="sec-head rv"><span class="sec-num">I.</span><h2>The Method</h2><span class="rule"></span></div>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <div class="prose rv">
      <p>Most prediction claims are told after the fact, from memory, by the person who
      benefits from the telling. The audit removes every one of those outs. A forecast
      here is written down, given a probability and a deadline, and cryptographically
      sealed <em>before</em> any outcome exists. When the deadline passes, an adjudicator
      who sees neither the forecaster nor the stated probability rules on the evidence.
      The result — hit or miss — goes on the record and never comes off.</p>
      <p class="dictum">“What feels true is a hypothesis. The world is the only referee.”</p>
      <p>The night is the condition, not the excuse. Everyone forecasts in fog; the
      question is whether you kept the score.</p>
      <p class="seal">The full definition is sealed in commit history:
      <a href="https://github.com/OccultusTheoretician/netz/blob/main/RETRO_PRESCIENT_AUDIT.md">RETRO_PRESCIENT_AUDIT.md</a></p>
    </div>
    <ol class="laws rv">
      <li><b>Sealed before the outcome.</b> Every projection is hashed into a commitment
      the day it is issued. Editing, softening, or deleting a forecast breaks the seal
      for the entire set.</li>
      <li><b>Falsifiable as written.</b> A stranger reading only the statement must be
      able to say happened or didn't. Anything that resolves however you feel about it
      is rejected at the gate.</li>
      <li><b>Blind adjudication.</b> The adjudicator sees neither forecaster nor stated
      probability, must cite evidence, and may return ambiguous.</li>
      <li><b>The record keeps its misses.</b> Hits and misses publish together,
      permanently. A ledger that can shed its failures is a marketing document.</li>
      <li><b>Under thirty resolutions, the score is noise.</b> The ledger says so on its
      own face until the record is deep enough to mean something.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="instruments">
  <div class="sec-head rv"><span class="sec-num">II.</span><h2>The Instruments</h2><span class="rule"></span></div>
  <div class="cards rv">
    <a class="card" href="ledger.html">
      <span class="card-k">Primary instrument</span>
      <span class="card-t">The KKR Ledger</span>
      <span class="card-d"><b>KKR is the Kaos Kontrol Report</b>, the daily forecasting
      stage that issues the projections. This is its ledger: every projection ever issued,
      open and resolved, hits and misses, Brier score and calibration table, segregated by
      the forecaster arm that issued it. The only surface here that constitutes evidence of
      skill.</span>
      <span class="card-go">Read the record →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="report.html#tab_wardesk">
      <span class="card-k">Verification instrument</span>
      <span class="card-t">The War Desk</span>
      <span class="card-d">Armed-conflict claims graded by who disagrees. A report is
      single-source until an <em>independently-biased</em> channel corroborates it; when
      enemies agree an event happened, it happened. Single-source claims are counted and
      withheld.</span>
      <span class="card-live" id="wd-live">Latest pull: —</span>
      <span class="card-top3" id="wd-top3"></span>
      <span class="card-go">Confirmed events →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="report.html">
      <span class="card-k">Collation feed</span>
      <span class="card-t">NETZ — Daily Report</span>
      <span class="card-d">Open-source collation under intelligence grammar: mechanical
      corroboration grading, standing requirements, convergence watch, a citation audit
      on every synthesized line.</span>
      <span class="card-go">Today's desk →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="kkr.html">
      <span class="card-k">Working surface · KKR</span>
      <span class="card-t">The Kaos Kontrol Report</span>
      <span class="card-d">The current issuance — sealed projections with deadlines,
      resolution criteria, and stated probabilities, committed before any outcome
      exists.</span>
      <span class="card-go">The open positions →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="KriegForeKaster.html">
      <span class="card-k">Scored order of battle</span>
      <span class="card-t">KriegForeKaster</span>
      <span class="card-d">Formations on a map where the unit of record is the claim, not
      the unit. Existence, composition, posture, position and command each carry their own
      grade, their own sources and their own date, and each expires on a published
      half-life &mdash; command at sixty days, position at fourteen. A claim past its
      half-life is not asserted wrong; it means nobody has checked recently, and the board
      greys it rather than showing it with the confidence of a fresh one. Claims worth
      arguing about are issued into the ledger and resolved hit or miss like any other
      projection.</span>
      <span class="card-live">US Army proving set live &mdash; every claim sourced, dated, and expiring on a published clock</span>
      <span class="card-go">The board &rarr;</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="https://github.com/OccultusTheoretician/voidsection">
      <span class="card-k">Sibling instrument</span>
      <span class="card-t">VoidSection™</span>
      <span class="card-d">The same discipline turned on institutions: the distance
      between the document and the conduct, scored under the Inversion Quotient.
      Pre-registered; no entity scored yet.</span>
      <span class="card-go">The gap engine →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="kraehes_kalls.html">
      <span class="card-k">Abduction log</span>
      <span class="card-t">Krähe's Kalls</span>
      <span class="card-d">The calls that fire mid-synthesis, sealed the instant they are
      spoken and held in the dark. Contents abyssal; the count is committed. Reveal is his
      alone — the misses stay bound.</span>
      <span class="card-go">The sealed nest →</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="standing">
  <div class="sec-head rv"><span class="sec-num">III.</span><h2>The Record</h2><span class="rule"></span></div>
  <div class="record-grid rv">
    <div class="standing">
      <p>This is an instrument being tested in public, not a validated one. Under thirty
      resolved predictions the score is noise — and the ledger says so on its own face.
      The record currently shows the machine <strong>missing more than it hits</strong>.</p>
      <p>That number is the credential. A desk that prints its own bad news is the only
      kind whose good news means anything.</p>
      <div class="tiefe" aria-label="Depth to statistical signal">
        <div class="tiefe-lbl"><span>Depth to signal</span><span id="tiefe-n">— / 30 resolved</span></div>
        <div class="tiefe-bar"><div class="tiefe-fill" id="tiefe-fill"></div>
          <div class="tiefe-mark" title="the noise floor"></div></div>
        <div class="tiefe-sub">The score means nothing until the floor. The bar says how far.</div>
      </div>
      <p class="close">Consistency is not correctness — resolution is.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="verdicts">
      <div class="verdicts-k">Latest verdicts — live from the ledger</div>
      <ul id="verdicts"><li class="pend">reading the record…</li></ul>
      <a class="card-go" href="ledger.html">Every verdict, permanently →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

